### PERF-004: Read-modify-write race condition on user file
**Severity:** High
**Location:** Lines 16-18

**Evidence:** The `/register` handler reads users.json (line 16), pushes a new user (line 17), and writes the file back (line 18). Under concurrent requests, two registrations can read the same state, each append their user, and overwrite each other — losing one registration. Even with async I/O, this pattern is inherently racy without locking.

