- **Description**: Every search request loads the **entire users table** into Node.js memory, then filters in application code. This is an O(n) full-table transfer on every request, where the database should be doing the filtering. With 100K users at ~1KB each, that's ~100MB transferred from DB to app per search request. The database has indexing capabilities (e.g., trigram indexes, `ILIKE`) that make this orders of magnitude cheaper.
