### PERF-002: Sequential Tool Execution Where Parallel Execution Is Possible
- **Rule ID**: PERF-002
- **Severity**: Medium
- **Category**: Concurrency Utilization / I/O Optimization
- **Location**: Lines 6-9 (`for...of` loop with `await executeTool`)

**Description**: When `response.toolCalls` contains multiple tool calls, each is executed sequentially via `await executeTool(call.name, call.args)` on line 7. If these tool calls are independent (which is typical — the LLM emits them in a single response precisely because they are parallel-eligible), this serializes I/O-bound work unnecessarily. With N tool calls each taking T milliseconds, the current approach takes O(N×T) instead of O(T).

